* Switched bench port with winding-current feedback to the existing trip latch.
* This fixture ties N and L to simulation ground. Logic supply collapse is
* represented by power-good inputs. No insulation or common-mode behavior.
.subckt PROTECTED_DAB P N H L PA PB SA SB PRI_OK SEC_OK ARM RUN ENP ENS VSENSE IP PMP SMP
.param LK=8u LM=851.84u NSEC=2 RP=0.06 RLO=9.5m RHI=9.5m IMAG0=0
Bcs IP 0 V=i(Ltransfer)
Xprotect IP PRI_OK SEC_OK ARM RUN ENP ENS VSENSE BENCH_PROTECT

* Inhibit both commands on each bridge. The secondary paths include separate
* timing-isolator delays and a local power-good veto. The command RC is a
* simplified switching-conductance transition, with no MOSFET Miller plateau.
Rsa SA sai 1k
Csa sai 0 18p
Rsb SB sbi 1k
Csb sbi 0 18p
Ba da 0 V={v(PA)*(v(ENP)>1.65)}
Bb db 0 V={v(PB)*(v(ENP)>1.65)}
Bc dc 0 V={v(sai)*(v(ENS)>1.65 && v(SEC_OK)>1.65)}
Bd dd 0 V={v(sbi)*(v(ENS)>1.65 && v(SEC_OK)>1.65)}
Ra da cpa 6.7
Rb db cpb 6.7
Rc dc csa 6.7
Rd dd csb 6.7
Caout cpa 0 2n
Cbout cpb 0 2n
Ccout csa 0 2n
Cdout csb 0 2n
Bpwm_p PMP 0 V={v(cpa)+v(cpb)}
Bpwm_s SMP 0 V={v(csa)+v(csb)}
.include dab-power.inc
.ends PROTECTED_DAB
